127:Td5e,**Challenges and practical solutions**

**Date:** 8 May 2025\
**Time:** 10:00 – 11:35 (CET)\
**Location:** Online via Microsoft Teams\
**Participation:** Free of charge, registration required via Eventbrite

## How can recyclate quality be reliably assessed?

What are the key challenges in recyclate use – and what practical solutions are available?

These questions take centre stage in the upcoming webinar **“Efficient Use of Recyclates – Challenges & Solutions”**, hosted by **plastship** on 8 May. The spotlight will be on a crucial topic for the plastics and recycling industry alike: **assessing recyclate quality** as the basis for efficient and sustainable use.

## Why you shouldn’t miss this webinar

This session is aimed at:

- Professionals in the plastics industry
- Recycling companies
- Decision-makers in the circular economy

The goal is to showcase practical solutions and best practices for the use of recyclates, while also facilitating dialogue and exchange among industry experts and participants.

> Our aim is to present actionable solutions and promote exchange between all stakeholders – so we can improve the efficiency and sustainability of the recyclate loop.

states **Andreas Bastian**.

## Programme overview

Participants can look forward to insights from experts at **Veridis**, **RAM**, **3S**, **SGS Fresenius** and **RIGK** who will share their experience and practical solutions. The topics covered range from advanced methods for recyclate quality assessment to key regulatory developments such as the Packaging and Packaging Waste Regulation (PPWR).

![](/images/cms/unbenannt-9-7af3cd.webp)

- *10:00 – 10:10:* **Welcome and introduction**\
  Opening remarks by plastship on the purpose of the webinar and the importance of recyclate efficiency within the circular economy.
- *10:10 – 10:50:* **Assessing recyclate quality – methods and technologies**\
  Experts from Veridis, RAM, 3S and SGS Fresenius will share practical insights into current recyclate testing methods, including polymer content analysis and quality measurement technologies.
- *10:50 – 11:10:* **Regulatory framework and certification**\
  RIGK and PlastCert will provide an overview of relevant legislation, with a focus on the Packaging and Packaging Waste Regulation (PPWR), and explain how the PlastCert certification system works in practice.
- *11:10 – 11:30:* **Discussion and exchange**\
  Interactive Q&A session with all speakers – an opportunity to ask specific questions and share perspectives.
- *11:30 – 11:35:* **Summary and outlook**\
  Key takeaways and a brief look at what's next in the field.

## Professional dialogue at eye level

> “We don’t just want to share information – we want to spark a conversation that leads to new ideas and long-term cooperation.”\
> – Mirco Gattinger, Marketing Manager at plastship

## Register now

Participation is free of charge, but registration via Eventbrite is required. All registered attendees will receive the Microsoft Teams link to join the session.

Join the discussion!

[Register here](https://www.eventbrite.de/e/efficient-use-of-recyclates-challenges-solutions-tickets-1299263334609)

If you have questions or suggestions, please contact me!

**Mirco Gattinger**, Marketing & Social Media Manager\
